  - name: "Link with the Lords of Magic"
    description: "A mysterious connection to the Lords of Magic, like a priest''s to his gods. Through it, unknown to him, he can animate and empower the Automatons. Known to him: he can draw on the P.P.E. reserves of The Three to create permanent magic weapons with Enchant Weapon (Minor), at half the normal P.P.E. cost to The Three. The link helps him learn his high level magic, and when a High Magus is killed The Three know instantly, roughly where (within 200 miles/320 km) and whether he suffered, but not how or by whom."
  - name: "Create Automaton (ritual)"
    description: "Exclusive to the High Magus (and a tiny handful of high level Lord Magi he has taught). Range: inside a magic circle. Duration: permanent. Time to cast: 48 hours. Saving throw: not applicable. P.P.E. cost by construct: 752 Infiltrator (infiltrator-automaton), 780 Ice Drake (ice-drake-automaton), 654 Earth Thunder (earth-thunder-automaton), 800 Fire Demon (fire-demon-automaton), 824 Battlelord (battlelord-automaton), 1008 Kilairgh (kilairgh-automaton), 1250 Colossus (colossus-automaton). Transforms an inert constructed body, which takes many months to build, into a mobile M.D.C. juggernaut. The magus intones the ritual for a full 48 hours: 100 P.P.E. to start it, 12-20 P.P.E. per hour throughout, and the balance at the end, meditating in between; he cannot eat, drink, sleep or do anything else, and any interruption ruins the ritual and loses all P.P.E. spent. For the Colossus he may have to draw on scores of people in a ritual or on a ley line nexus. Only the Lords of Magic can animate a finished body in 3D4 minutes."
  - name: "Bonding Ritual"
    description: "Exclusive to the High Magus. Range: inside a magic circle. Duration: permanent, until the Automaton is destroyed or the Controller slain. Time to cast: 24 hours. Saving throw: not applicable. P.P.E. cost: 20 from the High Magus to initiate it and 20 spent by the recipient. Performed only on a Battle Magus Controller, who spends the 24 hours in physical contact with the construct, usually in meditation, and afterwards controls its every movement as if it were his own body."
