extraction_notes: |
  - Transcribed from printed 79-82 (cache p080-p083); the bonus lines, the
    P.P.E. line, the ritual costs, the skill list and the XP ladder were read
    off renders. The ladder is the "Corrupt, High Magus" column on printed
    160, shared with the Corrupt; xp_table holds each band''s lower bound.
  - "All 11th/12th/13th/14th/15th level spells" are named lists, drawn on
    2026-09-26 from production: every general invocation (no tradition) of
    that spell level available to Rifts. Spells imported later at those levels
    are not added by themselves. Create Mummy (11) and Create Zombie (12) are
    left out because the Magi never study or practice Necromancy (printed 71).
    The level 2-5 grants are schedule entries whose count is the whole list,
    so the player takes every one; the level-two named seven are a list of
    their own.
  - Initial spells are stored under the catalog''s names: Dispel Magic Barrier
    is Dispel Magic Barriers, Teleport Lesser is Teleport: Lesser, Super
    Healing is Super-Healing. Healing Touch has no catalog row in any system
    and is NOT granted; it is recorded here.
  - Temporal Magic has no catalog rows, so the level 6+ alternative of two
    Temporal Magic spells is only in each entry''s note.
  - "Lore: Magic & Geomancy (+15%)" is the Lore: Magic row; the only geomancy
    lore row is Nightbane''s. "Armorer" in the Military list is Field Armorer &
    Munitions Expert.
  - The saves read: mind control +1 at levels 2, 4, 6, 8, 12 and 14; Horror
    Factor +1 at 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13 and 15; magic +1 at 1, 3, 7, 11 and
    15; illusions +1 at 1, 4, 6, 7, 9, 11, 13 and 15. Level one is in
    bonuses.saves and the rest in at_level. "Impervious to possession" has
    no save key and is prose.
  - Automaton Creation and the Bonding Ritual are special abilities, not
    catalog rows (the survey''s decision 4). The Automatons they create are
    vehicles rows, named by slug in the ritual''s text.
  - The body armor (50 M.D.C.) and spine helmet (45 M.D.C.) and the two
    magic weapons of choice have no catalog rows and stay in the Equipment
    section. A half dozen pens or markers is six pens.
  - men_of_arms is false: the book files the class under its "Magus O.C.C.s"
    heading (printed 70), a school of magic.
---

## Lore

The High Magus specializes in the most advanced and costly spell magic and rituals, with a focus on creation: enchanting weapons, making scrolls and talismans, creating golems and every Automaton, and the building and engineering of bridges, walls, bunkers and houses, along with healing and restoration. The Brotherhood of Creation is the smallest and most secretive of the three; fewer than a thousand High Magi are believed to live at Dweomer. They oversee many of the Techno-Wizard guilds and factories and planned and built the city.

More academic and philosophical than the other Magi, High Magi are compassionate and tolerant, very moral and ethical, and vulnerable to the sorrow of seeing others suffer. A builder rather than a warrior, the High Magus avoids combat, but his spells include Ensorcel, Soul Twist, Firequake, Meteor and Annihilate. They make excellent heroes and lawmen, champions of the innocent.

## Equipment

Clothes, uniform, ceremonial robes, utility belt, a canteen, backpack, knapsack, duffle bag, three small sacks, magnifying glass, binoculars, notebook, a half dozen pens or markers, portable computer, a flashlight, compass and pocket knife.

Standard High Magus body armor (50 M.D.C.) and spine helmet (45 M.D.C., 6-12 spikes, insect-like eyes and a beaded mouthpiece), of M.D.C. composite materials or magically created materials. Not a full environmental suit.

Weapons: two of choice, all magical. The High Magus can empower and enchant weapons and make Talismans and Scrolls.

Money: as an elite member of the Dweomer Defense Force he has a roomy four-bedroom apartment, meals, uniforms, healing and access to the laboratories, factories and academies, with a monthly salary of 3000 credits. Starts with 3D4x1,000 Universal Credits.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'high-magus');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'high-magus';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-high-magus-class.sql');
